<p>A drone strike caused a fire on Sunday at an electrical generator outside the inner perimeter of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in the Al Dhafra region of Abu Dhabi, UAE authorities said. Abu Dhabi&#x27;s media office said no injuries were reported, radiological safety levels were unaffected and precautionary measures had been taken. The UAE defence ministry said three drones entered the country from the direction of the western border and one reached the generator, and that investigations were under way to identify the source. The UAE foreign ministry condemned the attack, while no one immediately claimed responsibility.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/-81KdgKsoA7bQ4OAe4ry56AW_yTc1uKB0Lq8Lm4KoHpYDDtUROCFXwNXyP1t2bfXvpgOEFIJ-G3KQxOMT8GhU5IoAhG6iHIwUwG4F_6RWcFl0dGz0Ku7J6eW7nqqm-JNbQkGBRWF8i6hIO1pOANr-uYsqsNqyCwJJ5Cl3pgcmNebLAxVPnvUZUgQuJ56ne0-LaKRBJNa9W0iwk9VusBaKuxmIygsdLV1ui-Iwp_aaWvobECONWuwT0BZwvDp77LfxujV78ZAFuQUwNyRGg' alt='A general view of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in Abu Dhabi&#x27;s western Al Dhafra region.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Operational status: Authorities said plant operations were not affected by the fire.</li><li>Regional context: The strike followed weeks of stalled efforts to end the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran and restart Gulf shipping, while President Trump said Iran must act “fast”.</li></ul><blockquote>Military activity that threatens nuclear safety is unacceptable. - Rafael Grossi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UAE defence ministry: The ministry said two of the three drones were intercepted before the third hit near Barakah, and that it was investigating the source. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/fire-drone-strike-united-arab-emirates-uae-barakah-nuclear-plant/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>UAE foreign ministry: The ministry framed the strike as a “dangerous escalation,” “an unacceptable act of aggression” and a direct threat to national security. (<a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/uae-condemns-drone-strike-caused-fire-outside-nuclear-plant'>The New Arab</a>)</li><li>UAE presidential adviser Anwar Gargash: France 24 reported that Gargash appeared to refer to Iran and its regional proxy groups in his condemnation of the attack. (<a href='https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260517-drone-strike-sparks-a-fire-on-the-edge-of-uae-nuclear-facility'>France 24</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/17/fire-broke-out-after-drone-strike-near-uae-s-barakah-nuclear-power-plant_6753536_4.html'>Fire broke out after drone strike near UAE&#x27;s Barakah nuclear plant</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/a-drone-strike-causes-fire-outside-a-nuclear-power-plant-in-abu-dhabi/article70990120.ece'>Drone strike causes fire outside nuclear power plant in Abu Dhabi</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c4b786a6-55d4-4689-b19e-48a48f7946e6'>UAE says drone strike caused fire at nuclear plant</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353889/drone-targets-uae-nuclear-power-plant-straining-iran-war-ceasefire'>Drone targets UAE nuclear power plant, straining Iran war ceasefire</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy27pkj1l1o'>UAE reports strike near Abu Dhabi nuclear power plant</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/17/uae-blames-iran-or-its-proxies-for-drone-strike-fire-near-nuclear-plant'>UAE blames Iran or its proxies for drone strike fire near nuclear plant</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/drone-hits-uae-nuclear-power-plant-iaea-reports-normal-radiation-levels'>Drone hits UAE nuclear power plant: IAEA reports normal radiation levels</a> - france24.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-reports-drone-strike-at-nuclear-power-plant-as-iran-war-deadlock-endures'>UAE report